  "reasoning_content": "We need respond to user: \"Write a detailed tutorial on implementing a bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include a complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, and include tests. Continue with a worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and use meaningful prose and code.\"\n\nNeed produce final tutorial. Need think thoroughly. Need maybe code with OrderedDict LRU cache. Include complete class, tests. Edge cases: capacity <=0? missing keys? update timestamp. Could implement generic type? Python typing. Use OrderedDict move_to_end. Behavior: get(key) returns value or None/default; put(key, value, capacity?) updates existing or inserts; if capacity exceeded evict least recently used. Need discuss that OrderedDict move_to_end(last=False/True). If we treat most recently used at end, popitem(last=False) evicts oldest.\n\nNeed complete class. Could include __len__, __contains__, __getitem__, __setitem__, clear, peek, keys, values, items. Maybe optional default in get, capacity validation, max capacity int. Also support overwrite updating recency. Edge cases: zero capacity maybe either raise or store nothing. For robust: capacity < 0 raise; capacity == 0: get returns default, put no-op? But if user expects no storage. Could implement. Or require capacity > 0. To discuss edge cases maybe handle capacity <= 0. Need precise. Could implement with capacity = 0 means empty cache; put raises? Let's decide: Many bounded cache implementations require positive. But edge case discussion could include if max_size <=0: either error or no-op. I'd implement: capacity must be non-negative. If negative raise ValueError at construction. If zero: get returns default, put returns None, len 0. But if later set capacity? We could allow resize? Maybe not. Or include set_capacity that evicts if reduced. But not necessary. Could add for completeness? Keep tutorial focused.\n\nNeed include tests. Use unittest. Tests: miss returns None/default, stores and retrieves, updates existing without increasing size, evicts LRU when capacity exceeded, get moves key to MRU, put updates existing key, capacity zero, negative capacity error, contains, len, del? If include __delitem__, need eviction on delete? Not affect LRU? Deleting key doesn't make others MRU? OrderedDict remove; if delete MRU, next LRU remains. Need __delitem__ remove if exists else KeyError. Could",
